Importantly, the substantive conclusions about our core hypotheses are stable across models: transitivity remains positive and strong, and inPop remains negative. In Model 2, reciAct is negative (Estimate = -0.460, SE = 0.104), suggesting the update captures additional reciprocated-degree structure that was not well reproduced by Model 1.:contentReference[oaicite:13]{index=13}
